        "collapse_gXh4yj": {
          "type": "collapse",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<p>Why start with the bathroom?</p>",
            "content": "<p>Bathrooms are built around permanent decisions—mirrors, cabinetry, tile, fixtures, and plumbing. They are hard to change, even as daily behaviors inside them already have evolved.<br/><br/>As a designer working with bathroom products and spaces for years, I wonder:<br/><br/><strong>Could a smaller object help an existing space keep up?</strong><br/><br/>TapNest is our first answer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapse_bQbcgr": {
          "type": "collapse",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<p>Isn’t TapNest just a simple phone holder?</p>",
            "content": "<p>Not quite. Holding your phone was only half the problem.<br/><br/>Most phone holders were designed as temporary accessories. They worked technically, but took up space, felt visually disconnected from home vibe.<br/><br/>We wanted TapNest to behave more like <strong>part of the room</strong>: something that could<strong> </strong>stay, belong, and support different routines without prescribing one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapse_eCWmQm": {
          "type": "collapse",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<p>Is OORA only about phones?</p>",
            "content": "<p><strong>No.</strong> OORA looks for small habits that have changed, but are still poorly supported by the spaces around them.<br/><br/>We create thoughtful objects that <strong>help familiar spaces adapt to you.</strong></p>"
          }
        }
      },
